phydrax-meshcore is an independently authored C++20 implementation informed by
published robust-geometry algorithms: Shewchuk adaptive floating-point
expansions and predicates; Simulation of Simplicity and lifted-coordinate
perturbations for Delaunay and regular triangulations; half-space polytope
clipping informed by r3d; triangle-contact classification informed by Guigue and
Devillers; and Delaunay refinement after Ruppert, Chew, and Shewchuk.

No upstream source code, including the public-domain predicates.c, is copied,
translated, or redistributed in this package. Gmsh, Mmg, fTetWild/wildmeshing,
Manifold, Open3D, OpenVDB, VoroCrust, Omega_h, TIOGA, METIS, SciPy/Qhull, and
OCCT/OCP are independent optional provider, comparison, or interchange
boundaries and are not bundled in phydrax-meshcore.
